License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
License File: LICENCE-LGPL-2.1.txt
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

Local changes: GN build and desktop config.h; omitted examples, tests,
utilities and console-platform build directories. The client error decoder
accepts COPYCHUNK failures with an IOCTL response body (MS-SMB2 3.3.5.15.6)
so the worker can handle the server status and retry smaller ranges.
Non-Windows builds use GNU C11 for upstream typeof/statement expressions in
alloc.c and dcerpc.c. Windows retains the upstream _MSC_VER fallback.
The library target opts out of Chromium's unsafe-buffers Clang plugin for
upstream C pointer-based buffers; crFiles application targets retain the check.
NTLMSSP authentication; no Kerberos, SMB1 or optional system libraries.
Only the crFiles SMB worker uses this library.

Redistributors must retain the license and provide the corresponding library
source and relinking materials required by LGPL 2.1 when statically linked.
The full library source is retained here; keep the exact crFiles source/build
configuration and linkable object files with each distributed binary release.
